        "passed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "uncertain write: a hung WCS offer quarantines, the lock is retained, inspection restores it, observation resolves the write",
        "passed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "child exit: the dead run's lock is adopted only with its nonce and no live host, then restored after inspection",
        "passed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "undeclared PLC fault stops held and is refused as outside the recorded paths",
        "passed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "a run held at the stopped baseline needs no reconciliation and is not written",
        "passed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "classification: recorded overload and start-feedback paths, late commit settlement, and refusals",
        "passed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "read-only inspection gate refuses every write until an explicit authorization",
        "passed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "recovery distinguishes a recorded child exit from a reused PID, disconnect or foreign nonce",
        "passed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "live commissioning qualification rejects missing, slow, empty and late-expiry evidence",
        "passed": true
      }
    ]
  },
  "establishes": [
    "The zero-model harness drives the real CampaignRuntime and isolated child through preconditions, read-only baseline, normal sort, six lease cases (incl. expiry under a 1.5 s parent stall), a declared overload fault and clean shutdown, and verifies the final state read-only",
    "Refusal before any PLC write: held lock, unclean baseline, live-mode test hooks, missing live pins",
    "A run that stops after writing records held-state.json: exact applied image, boot, epoch, sequence, in-flight commit/commands, uncertain writes, item/completion state, ownership and evidence hashes",
